  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, lattice existence construction.

    <item>Status: draft; independent mathematics and Lean correspondence
    reviews pending.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/rg-horizon-geometry.tex>,
    especially Proposition <verbatim|prop:ex-lattice-horizon-roll> and
    equations <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-horizon-*>.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
    (<verbatim|source/upstream.json>).

    <item>This unit proves the finite block completion in ordinary matrix
    algebra, expands the producer route to the actual horizon and tower
    costs, and records the path-to-root periodization. It does not claim to
    prove the upstream bed, flight, or path price estimates outside the cited
    supplier chain.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Inputs and notation><label|inputs-and-notation>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Symbol>>|<cell|<strong|Meaning
  and normalization>>|<cell|<strong|Source
  correspondence>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|H,H'>>|<cell|Adjacent fine/coarse
  beds; <verbatim|J=H.full p f>, <verbatim|J'=H'.full p' c> are the full root
  maps, including the direct block.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Precision.Bed.full>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PREC/Stacks.lean>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|W,W'>>|<cell|Finite-torus
  amended metrics <verbatim|J\<#1D40\>J>, <verbatim|J'\<#1D40\>J'>; inverses
  <verbatim|R,R'>.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Precision.Floor.roots>,
  <verbatim|.inverse>, <verbatim|.symmetric>, same
  path>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|D_f,D_c>>|<cell|First coboundary from 1-forms
  to 2-forms on the fine/coarse tori; <verbatim|d\<#2082\>D_c=0>.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Exterior.d
  1>, <verbatim|YM.Exterior.d 2>; <verbatim|YM.Work.F09.answer>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|T,A\<#2080\>>>|<cell|Actual
  installed two-form and one-form flight transports; <verbatim|\\bar T> is
  the actual conditional mean.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Precision.Towers.Diagonal.transport>,
  <verbatim|.stays>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|Z>>|<cell|<verbatim|R' \<minus\>
  T\<#1D40\>RT \<minus\> k\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\> D_cD_c\<#1D40\>>, the
  actual remainder in the roll factorization.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Craft.defect>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.F09.answer>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|P>>|<cell|Three-form
  factor with <verbatim|W'ZW'=D\<#2082\>\<#1D40\>P\<#1D40\>PD\<#2082\>>; its
  existence and strip/reach bounds are flight
  receipts.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Craft.Bleeps>, <verbatim|YM.Craft.Opens>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.F09.answer>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|L>>|<cell|Odd block
  side; costs retain explicit powers of <verbatim|L\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>>.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.RG.Ratio>,
  <verbatim|YM.Precision.Towers.Deep>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|D_r>>|<cell|Finite
  exponential strip cost of the exterior coboundary stencil from r-forms to
  (r+1)-forms, with the cover norm <verbatim|size(z)=sum_a
  \|z_a\|>.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.F08.stencilCost>,
  <verbatim|.strip_stencil>>>>>>

  The manuscript's matrix proposition assumes exactly the two transport
  identities, symmetric invertible bed metrics, and the stated curvature
  factorization. The selected flight and bed producers supply those premises.
  No spectral positivity assumption is needed in the block calculation beyond
  invertibility of the stated metrics and the factorization itself.

