  profile, kernel, length schedule, and horizon receipt.>>>>>

  <section|Actual producer chain and remaining
  assumptions><label|actual-producer-chain-and-remaining-assumptions>

  The mathematical horizon supplier is <verbatim|YM.Next.Free.retained_support>.
  Its input is a kernel and a sheet fixing that kernel; it constructs common
  <verbatim|Catalog> and map prices. For each actual level schedule whose
  kernel and stage match the sheet and whose numerical <verbatim|Credit>
  bounds hold, it uses <verbatim|shelves> to build the actual-cutoff family
  of beds and initial towers, then <verbatim|YM.Bid.pinning> to produce a
  retained horizon with <verbatim|Suffices> bounds. The <verbatim|Catalog> is
  itself produced by <verbatim|YM.Next.Free.pledges> from the one-flight
  frontiers and bed price construction, not a free choice of a new
  trajectory. The detailed upstream analytic receipts in those frontiers and
  the public payment that supplies <verbatim|Credit> are outside this section
  and remain explicit inputs to the larger construction.

  The public selected-run route begins with
  <verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>, which calls the preselected
  quote/order/numeric selector. <verbatim|YM.Integration.ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.on_run>
  converts its selected paid numerical receipts to the actual levels and
  horizon; <verbatim|.of_preselection> packages those receipts without
  replacing <verbatim|R.family.path.levels> or <verbatim|R.alloy.B.M>. The
  public flat-sector route additionally travels through
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.again>, the actual full-volume
  <verbatim|ahead> producer and its garden/Mauve path. No neighboring
  Cook/Multi proof interface was substituted. The exact world and non-linear
  inputs are crosswalked in their respective evidence units.

  For the path identity, the local proof uses the actual mathematical inputs
  <verbatim|Attached> and <verbatim|PathData.Bounds>.
  <verbatim|Attached.layout> identifies every fixed cover-displacement fiber;
  <verbatim|Bounds.rows> gives weighted absolute summability, so all infinite
  regroupings are legitimate. The selected-history route explicitly produces
  attachment at all cutoff/level/period triples. The inspected
  <verbatim|on_same> and <verbatim|heatSame> statements do not themselves
  list the weighted row-bound receipt; it must be supplied by the
  corresponding paid path input before the regrouping is applied. This
  section does not infer it from the finite block identities.

  <section|Literature and editorial decisions><label|literature-and-editorial-decisions>

  No external theorem is used for the finite matrix completion; the proof is
  an explicit finite-dimensional calculation. The row-cost estimate uses only
  the exponential-weight convolution inequality: for absolutely summable
  matrix kernels, the weighted row sum of a composition is at most the
  product of the two weighted row sums, with one finite sum over each
  intermediate label. The manuscript writes out the actual factors and counts
  for the order-two tower construction. Formal helper lemmas are grouped by
  their mathematical roles (finite matrix completion, stencil convolution,
  and path periodization).

